/// Map methods that extend the built-in map operations.
///
/// A map holds key-value pairs. `m[k]` reads the value stored under `k` and
/// raises `unknown_map_key` when there is none; `m[k] = v` adds the entry or
/// replaces its value. The built-in methods `m.len()`, `m.contains(k)`,
/// `m.remove(k)`, `m.keys()` and `m.values()` cover the rest, and a map
/// iterates its keys (`for k in m { ... }`). This module adds the methods
/// below in an `impl map` block. It is part of the prelude, so they need no
/// import.
///
/// The methods are polymorphic through Candela's compile-time
/// monomorphization: a single definition specializes to whatever key and value
/// types the call site uses.
///
/// This module is pure Candela and compiles into a `.cdlb` artifact that runs
/// under `candela-vm` with no dynamic library.

impl map {
    /// True when the map has no entries.
    fn is_empty(self) {
        return self.len() == 0;
    }

    /// The value stored under `k` as `Some`, or `None` when the map holds no
    /// such key. `m.get(k).unwrap_or(fallback)` reads with a fallback.
    fn get(self, k) => if self.contains(k) { Some(self[k]) } else { None };
}
